\name{cellucid_camera_framing}
\alias{cellucid_camera_framing}
\title{Frame cells with the camera}
\usage{
cellucid_camera_framing(viewer, azimuth, categories, elevation, field, fill = 0.8, view)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{azimuth}{Degrees around the vertical axis the camera looks from (3D views); omitted, the view's own. 90 apart is a quarter turn. A number. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{categories}{Only these categories of the field; they are also framed together. Omitted, every category the view shows. A vector or list of text (at least 1 character) (at least 1 item, each once). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{elevation}{Degrees above (positive) or below the subject the camera looks from (3D views); omitted, the view's own. A number (at least -85, at most 85). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{field}{A categorical field whose categories to frame, each on its own. A named list. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does). \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The column name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{Exactly \code{"obs"}. Required.}}}
\item{fill}{How much of the frame the cells fill across or up: 0.8 a close shot with a margin, 0.4 the subject with its surroundings. A number (more than 0, at most 1). Default \code{0.8}, the viewer's own.}
\item{view}{The view: "View N" as the Compare views list numbers it; the selected view when left out. Text. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{direction}, \code{embedding}, \code{field}, \code{frame}, \code{groups}, \code{navigation} (The mode of the cameras: orbit for 3D, planar (facing the x\ifelse{latex}{<U+2013>}{–}y plane) for 1D and 2D), \code{not_shown} (Categories with no cell the view shows (filtered or hidden)), \code{together} (The categories named, in one shot), \code{view}, \code{whole}. Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
Where cells sit in a view and cameras that frame them, seen from a direction: the whole view, each category of a field (or those named), and those named together. Nothing moves; give a camera to camera_set or camera_path_keyframe_add. It frames the view as it is laid out now (side by side, a view is narrower): arrange the views first.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{camera.framing} (Camera). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_camera_framing(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
